WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.136 --> 00:00:03.689
-Our first guest is a
six-time Oscar nominee,

00:00:03.689 --> 00:00:07.240
starring in the new film
"Dear Evan Hansen,"

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.643
which opens in theaters
Friday, September 24th.

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:13.779
Here is Amy Adams!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:16.515
Ah! I love you! Hi, Amy!

00:00:16.515 --> 00:00:18.150
-Hi. It's good to see you.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.786
-You look great.
Welcome back, welcome back.

00:00:20.786 --> 00:00:23.756
Thank you for being here.
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:26.559
I wish I was there in person.
I miss you guys.

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.594
-I know. Yeah, I know.
We miss you, too.

00:00:28.594 --> 00:00:30.330
I miss seeing your daughter,
as well.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.331
-Yeah, she was really bummed

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:34.233
we weren't going to be there
in person.

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:36.402
She loves to go backstage
and eat all the treats.

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:38.471
So she was really --
I mean, she loves you.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.473
-Yeah, of course, she doesn't
care about me at all, yeah.

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.742
-No, she doesn't.
-She just wants the treats.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.611
-She just wants
that Tonight Dough.

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:47.680
Ever since you guys
gave her that, that's it.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.715
-Our ice cream,
the Tonight Dough,

00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:51.650
which is the greatest.
Do we have any?

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:54.420
Usually, we have a fake pint.
Here's a fake one now.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.656
That's our --
She loves Tonight Dough?

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:58.691
This is it.
-It is so good.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:01.727
-This is the best.
-It is the best. The best.

00:01:01.727 --> 00:01:04.864
-How old is she now?
-She's 11.

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.300
-No.
-She is 11, yeah.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:10.970
-That's wild.
-Yeah, 11 going on like 45.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.372
So, I'm sure I'm gonna
get in trouble

00:01:13.372 --> 00:01:15.675
for saying that, actually.
-Really?

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:17.877
-Well, she's at that age
where everything I do

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:20.079
embarrasses her,
which is fun for me.

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:21.881
I'm sure
it's very painful for her,

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:24.717
but it's fun for me.
-That's wild.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.553
I've known her
her whole life then, huh?

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:28.955
-You have, yeah.
-That's wild, that's amazing.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:31.023
Well, please tell her
I said hello,

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:32.792
or I can just say hi
if she's watching.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.293
-I will.
-Yeah, please.

00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:35.962
I'm going to send her
a case of this, by the way,

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:37.596
so she gets it --
-Oh, my gosh.

00:01:37.596 --> 00:01:41.501
Yeah, I'm doing that because,
yeah, tell her I love her.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:45.037
You had a very exciting summer
because you filmed

00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:48.207
the sequel to "Enchanted,"
and I knew that.

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:49.675
You told me that you
were going to do.

00:01:49.675 --> 00:01:51.210
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.746
The first one was giant,
and everyone is back for this.

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:57.183
What can you tell me
about the sequel?

00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:00.086
-It was a lot of fun to film.
We filmed it in Ireland.

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:02.388
There is -- Everyone is back.

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:05.324
We also have
great additions to the cast.

00:02:05.324 --> 00:02:06.993
We have Maya Rudolph.
-Yes!

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:10.096
-Some other great people. Yeah.
-Maya!

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:13.465
How is Maya! She's the best.
-Oh, she's amazing.

00:02:13.465 --> 00:02:16.468
-She's so fun, right?
-She is so great in it.

00:02:16.468 --> 00:02:17.670
She plays the baddie,

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:20.606
so we get to have
a lot of fun together.

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:24.476
There's a lot more singing
and a lot more dancing.

00:02:24.476 --> 00:02:27.480
-Yeah, great.
-Which was humbling. Yeah.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:30.449
-Humbling, for you?
-Well, yeah.

00:02:30.449 --> 00:02:32.318
The last time I really danced

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.153
as much as I'm required
to dance in this,

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:38.324
I was in my 20s,
and now I'm not in my 20s.

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:41.394
And it feels different
in your 40s.

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:43.562
-It really does, yeah.
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:43.562 --> 00:02:46.298
In my heart, I look like I'm
in my 20s when I'm dancing,

00:02:46.298 --> 00:02:48.234
and then I would watch playback
and be like, "Whoa,

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.537
that's not the same."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.537 --> 00:02:52.872
-You can do everything.

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:55.174
It is Broadway week
here on our show,

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:58.444
and I know you love Broadway.
I mean, how happy are you

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.380
that Broadway is back?
This is a giant thing.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:03.949
-It's amazing.
I start talking really fast

00:03:03.949 --> 00:03:05.985
when I talk about Broadway,
because I totally turn into

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:09.521
that high school student who
their whole life is musicals.

00:03:09.521 --> 00:03:12.691
If you want to feel good
about things in the world,

00:03:12.691 --> 00:03:14.627
just watch the casts returning,

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:15.994
because it's
the most joyful thing.

00:03:15.994 --> 00:03:18.164
I've been on a deep dive of
watching everybody

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:21.400
celebrate the return,
and it's so uplifting.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.768
And I'm so excited.

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:24.336
And I saw Ben last night
on the show.

00:03:24.336 --> 00:03:26.038
He was brilliant.
I could keep going.

00:03:26.038 --> 00:03:27.974
I start getting real fast-talky.
-I like when you get chatty.

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:30.910
It's fun 'cause we have
a rehearsal here,

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:33.112
and everyone is trying
to not get choked up

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:36.081
of how much we missed
these talented people

00:03:36.081 --> 00:03:39.585
for almost two years.
It's like, "Gosh!"

00:03:39.585 --> 00:03:42.355
And, man, oh, man, support.
Please go get tickets

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:44.323
to any Broadway show
you can possibly see.

00:03:44.323 --> 00:03:46.092
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:49.428
It's just the greatest.
But you're about to

00:03:49.428 --> 00:03:52.064
make your debut
in the West End in London

00:03:52.064 --> 00:03:55.235
at "The Glass Menagerie."
-I am, yes.

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:59.638
This is exciting.
-It's really exciting.

00:03:59.638 --> 00:04:01.707
I think, you know,
during this time

00:04:01.707 --> 00:04:03.476
where we didn't have
live theater,

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:05.945
I really realized
how much I missed it,

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:08.014
not juice being
an audience member

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:10.216
but that exchange of energy
that happens in theater,

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:12.051
live audiences
like you have there,

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:14.219
that's just so unique,
and it's just

00:04:14.219 --> 00:04:15.454
something
I want to be a part of.

00:04:15.454 --> 00:04:18.358
-Yeah, you got a little "Whoo!"
from someone.

00:04:18.358 --> 00:04:19.725
-Whoo!
-We have a full audience here.

00:04:19.725 --> 00:04:23.662
Yeah. There's nothing like it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:23.662 --> 00:04:27.834
-Miss it.
-Do you rehearse now,

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:30.470
or how does it go into it
schedulewise?

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:32.338
How do you do it?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:35.408
We will rehearse,
and we open in may.

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:37.442
-Wow.
-Yeah, I'm nervous.

00:04:37.442 --> 00:04:40.680
I have so much respect
for the craft of stage acting

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:43.015
and musicals and
the eight shows a week,

00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:46.085
and I just look forward
to the challenge.

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:47.954
-I want to talk about
your new movie,

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:49.555
"Dear Evan Hansen"
when we come back.

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:51.257
More with Amy Adams
when we come back!

